## The reference frame for clipframe_narrow.rib: the same scene at the same
## 200 pixels per unit, widened to 960x600 by ScreenWindow -2.4 2.4 -1.5 1.5.
## Narrow pixel (x, y) is this frame's pixel (x + 160, y + 100). This frame
## clips the wall at its own left edge, narrow column -160, so inside the
## compared region its pixels do not depend on how the clipper colours a
## clip vertex.
Display "clipframe_wide.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 960 600 1
ScreenWindow -2.4 2.4 -1.5 1.5
Projection "perspective" "fov" [40]
Clipping 0.5 60
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.2]
LightSource "pointlight" 2 "intensity" [30] "from" [-1 0.5 4]
Sides 2
Color [0.5 0.7 0.9]
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [1]
Polygon "P" [-2.5 -1.5 -4  -2.5 -1.5 20  -2.5 1.5 20  -2.5 1.5 -4]
WorldEnd
